@prompt
Hazel supports labeled tuples, which let you associate labels with tuple elements — giving an ordered version of records. They also support projection by label:

```hazel
let pet = (name="Fido", age=4, species="dog") in
pet.name
```

# Task

Complete the labeled tuple below so that the x-coordinate equals the y-coordinate.

@hint
Pick any x and y as long as they're the same

@reference
### Labeled Tuple Projection
Access a field of a labeled tuple with `.`:
```hazel
let pet =
(name="Fido", 
age=4, 
species="dog") in
pet.name
```


@hints
Make sure they're the same and both floats

@code
type Point = (x=Float, y=Float) in

let p : Point = ¿ in
p

@test
test p.x == p.y end
